menu "IMX708 video example: board"

    config EXAMPLE_CAM_POWER_EN_GPIO
        int "GPIO that powers the camera module (-1 if none)"
        range -1 54
        default -1
        help
            Some boards route a GPIO to the camera connector's power-enable
            line (CAM_IO0 on the Raspberry Pi pinout), which switches the
            module's own regulators on and releases its reset. Until that GPIO
            is driven high the IMX708 is unpowered: nothing answers on I2C,
            and the I2C driver reports "clear bus failed" because the module's
            pull-ups are dead too.

            -1 for boards that power the connector permanently, such as the
            Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6. 0 on the Wireless-Tag WT9932P4-TINY,
            whose BSP drives IO0 high before touching the camera.

endmenu
